   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to extending the authority of the department of environmental conservation to manage fish",
    "basePrintNo": "S6988",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6988-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-1303, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6988\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to extending the authority of the department of environmental\nconservation to manage fish\n\nPurpose of the Bill:\n\nThis bill would extend the regulatory authority of the Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation (DEC) to manage fish.\n\nSummary of Provisions:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Environmental Conservation Law (ECL)\n§ 11-1303 to extend, until December 31, 2018 DEC's authority to fix by\nregulation measures for the management of fish, except marine species\nregulated under ECL Article 13.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nExisting Law:\n\nECL § 11-1303 grants DEC regulatory authority to manage fish until\nDecember 31, 2014. Prior Legislative History:  DEC's regulatory\nauthority to manage fish was last extended by Chapter 425 of the Laws\nof 2011.\n\nStatement in Support:\n\nECL § 11-0303 authorizes DEC to set open seasons, size and catch\nlimits, and the manner of taking of all species of fish, except marine\nfish. If this authority is not extended beyond the current sunset date\nof December 31, 2014, the existing regulations on the seasons, bag\nlimits, and manner of taking for freshwater fish would no longer be\nenforceable and there would be no oversight of the taking of\nfreshwater fish in State waters. Extending DEC's authority to regulate\nfreshwater fish would ensure continuity in the protection of the\nState's freshwater fish resources.\n\nBudget Implications:\n\nNone.\n\nLocal Impact:\n\nThe bill would have no impact on local governments.\n\nEffective Date:\n\nThe bill would take effect immediately.\n\n",
